#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "PARCAT1 is a BDS parameter-category variable, no place in an occurrence dataset. Since Fix #270 (ruling M2-D3) the Check tests the variable NAME: PARCAT1 matches the PARCAT family regex ^PARCAT([1-9]|[1-9][0-9])$ and the rule - routed as Variable Metadata Check / Record via evaluateMetadataNative - emits exactly ONE finding for that one offending column, pinned by variable_name (no row= pin: Violation.row carries the colIndex). No further column added: under per-variable evaluation every extra prohibited column is another finding."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=PARCAT1
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col AEDECOD  type=Char
col PARCAT1  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | SEVERITY
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | NAUSEA | SEVERITY
